IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- coa28-part46.l4: Part 46 (General supplementary provisions), ss 1288-1297 of the Companies Act 2006,
-- lines 18531-18594 of ukpga-2006-46.txt (a plain-text rendering from legislation.gov.uk; not the official text).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every answer is MAYBE BOOLEAN (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING) unless a
-- comment says otherwise; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words (FALSE-kind comments),
-- NOTHING where it does not (NOTHING-kind comments). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Nouns of this module: the procedure type (ss 1289-1292), the interval type that ss 1291(2) and Schedule 1A
-- para 24(8) both count over, and the kinds of enactment (s 1293).

-- =========================================================================================================
-- ss 1288 to 1292: regulations and orders
-- =========================================================================================================

-- The four ways the Act says regulations and orders can be subject to Parliament.
DECLARE `s 1288 procedure for regulations or orders` IS ONE OF
    `s 1289 negative resolution procedure`
    `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure`
    `s 1291 approval after being made`
    `s 1292(3) no Parliamentary procedure prescribed`

-- ---- s 1288 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18534 | Except as otherwise provided, regulations and orders under this Act shall be made by statutory instrument.
@ref s 1288 Regulations and orders: statutory instrument (src:18534)
GIVEN `the Act otherwise provides for the regulations or order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1288 the regulations or order under this Act must be made by statutory instrument` MEANS
    IF `the Act otherwise provides for the regulations or order`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as otherwise provided, regulations and orders under this Act shall be made by statutory instrument"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 1289 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18536 | Where regulations or orders under this Act are subject to “negative resolution procedure” the statutory instrument containing the regulations or order shall be subject to annulment in pursuance of a resolution of either House of Parliament.
@ref s 1289 Regulations and orders: negative resolution procedure (src:18536)
GIVEN procedure IS A `s 1288 procedure for regulations or orders`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1289 the statutory instrument is subject to annulment in pursuance of a resolution of either House of Parliament` MEANS
    CONSIDER procedure
    WHEN `s 1289 negative resolution procedure` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where regulations or orders under this Act are subject to “negative resolution procedure” the statutory instrument containing the regulations or order shall be subject to annulment" (a failed "where")

-- ---- s 1290 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "must not be made unless" is a bar: JUST TRUE means the bar holds now, JUST FALSE means it does not.
-- src:18538 | Where regulations or orders under this Act are subject to “affirmative resolution procedure” the regulations or order must not be made unless a draft of the statutory instrument containing them has been laid before Parliament and approved by a resolution of each House of Parliament.
@ref s 1290 Regulations and orders: affirmative resolution procedure (src:18538)
GIVEN procedure IS A `s 1288 procedure for regulations or orders`
      `a draft of the statutory instrument containing them has been laid before Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the draft has been approved by a resolution of each House of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1290 the regulations or order are barred from being made` MEANS
    CONSIDER procedure
    WHEN `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure` THEN
        IF `a draft of the statutory instrument containing them has been laid before Parliament` AND `the draft has been approved by a resolution of each House of Parliament`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be made unless a draft of the statutory instrument containing them has been laid before Parliament and approved by a resolution of each House of Parliament" (the "unless" is met)
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where regulations or orders under this Act are subject to “affirmative resolution procedure”" (a failed "where")

-- ---- s 1291 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The nouns for counting: a period of time during which Parliament was dissolved or prorogued, or both Houses
-- were adjourned. Days are inclusive: `first day` and `last day` are both days on which the time was running.
DECLARE `s 1291(2) kind of interval` IS ONE OF
    `s 1291(2) Parliament dissolved or prorogued`
    `s 1291(2) both Houses adjourned`

DECLARE `s 1291(2) interval` HAS
    `s 1291(2) first day of the interval` IS A DATE
    `s 1291(2) last day of the interval` IS A DATE
    `s 1291(2) kind of the interval` IS A `s 1291(2) kind of interval`

-- src:18540 | (1) Regulations or orders under this Act that are subject to “approval after being made”—
-- src:18541 | (a) must be laid before Parliament after being made, and
@ref s 1291(1)(a) Regulations and orders: approval after being made (src:18540-18541)
GIVEN `they have been laid before Parliament after being made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1291(1)(a) the requirement to lay the regulations or order before Parliament after being made has been met` MEANS
    IF `they have been laid before Parliament after being made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be laid before Parliament after being made" (a bare "must" not yet done: fork F3 in NOTES.md)

-- (2): "no account shall be taken of any time during which Parliament is dissolved or prorogued or during which
-- both Houses are adjourned for more than four days". Fork F1 in NOTES.md: "more than four days" is counted inclusively
-- (first and last day both count), so an adjournment of 10 to 14 January (five days) is disregarded and one of 10 to 13
-- (four days) is not.
-- src:18543 | (2) In reckoning the period of 28 days no account shall be taken of any time during which Parliament is dissolved or prorogued or during which both Houses are adjourned for more than four days.
@ref s 1291(2) Regulations and orders: approval after being made (src:18543)
GIVEN interval IS A `s 1291(2) interval`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1291(2) no account is taken of the time in the interval` MEANS
    CONSIDER interval's `s 1291(2) kind of the interval`
    WHEN `s 1291(2) Parliament dissolved or prorogued` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1291(2) both Houses adjourned` THEN
        IF (Day (interval's `s 1291(2) last day of the interval`)) MINUS (Day (interval's `s 1291(2) first day of the interval`)) PLUS 1 GREATER THAN 4
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "both Houses are adjourned for more than four days"

@ref s 1291(2) Regulations and orders: approval after being made (src:18543)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      intervals IS A LIST OF `s 1291(2) interval`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1291(2) the day falls in a time that is not taken into account` MEANS
    any (GIVEN i YIELD isInterval i) intervals
    WHERE
        isInterval i MEANS
                `the day` AT LEAST i's `s 1291(2) first day of the interval`
            AND `the day` AT MOST i's `s 1291(2) last day of the interval`
            AND `s 1291(2) no account is taken of the time in the interval` i EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The day on which the n-th day that counts falls, counting from `the day` as day 1 and skipping days that are
-- not taken into account. Used for the 28 days of s 1291(1)(b) and the 40 days of Schedule 1A para 24(7).
@ref s 1291(2) Regulations and orders: approval after being made (src:18543)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the number of days to count` IS A NUMBER
      intervals IS A LIST OF `s 1291(2) interval`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1291(2) the day on which the last of the days to count falls` MEANS
    IF `s 1291(2) the day falls in a time that is not taken into account` `the day` intervals
    THEN `s 1291(2) the day on which the last of the days to count falls` (`the day` PLUS 1) `the number of days to count` intervals
    ELSE IF `the number of days to count` AT MOST 1
         THEN `the day`
         ELSE `s 1291(2) the day on which the last of the days to count falls` (`the day` PLUS 1) (`the number of days to count` MINUS 1) intervals

-- Fork F2 in NOTES.md: "28 days beginning with the day on which they were made" counts the day of making as day 1, so the
-- last day is the made day plus 27 (plus the days not counted).
-- src:18542 | (b) cease to have effect at the end of 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made unless during that period they are approved by resolution of each House.
@ref s 1291(1)(b) Regulations and orders: approval after being made (src:18542)
GIVEN `the day on which they were made` IS A DATE
      intervals IS A LIST OF `s 1291(2) interval`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1291(1)(b) the last day of the 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made` MEANS
    `s 1291(2) the day on which the last of the days to count falls` `the day on which they were made` 28 intervals

@ref s 1291(1)(b) Regulations and orders: approval after being made (src:18542)
GIVEN `the day on which they were made` IS A DATE
      intervals IS A LIST OF `s 1291(2) interval`
      `the day the question is asked about` IS A DATE
      `the day on which each House had approved them` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1291(1)(b) the regulations or order have ceased to have effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day the question is asked about` AT MOST lastDay
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cease to have effect at the end of 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made" (the end of the period has not come)
        IF approvedInTime
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless during that period they are approved by resolution of each House"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        lastDay MEANS `s 1291(1)(b) the last day of the 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made` `the day on which they were made` intervals
        approvedInTime MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which each House had approved them`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST approval THEN approval AT MOST lastDay

DECLARE `s 1291(3) thing` IS ONE OF
    `s 1291(3)(a) anything previously done under them or it`
    `s 1291(3)(b) the making of new regulations or a new order`
    `s 1291(3) something else`

-- src:18544 | (3) The regulations or order ceasing to have effect does not affect—
-- src:18545 | (a) anything previously done under them or it, or
-- src:18546 | (b) the making of new regulations or a new order.
@ref s 1291(3) Regulations and orders: approval after being made (src:18544-18546)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 1291(3) thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1291(3) the regulations or order ceasing to have effect affects the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 1291(3) something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not affect— (a) anything previously done under them or it, or (b) the making of new regulations or a new order"
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The regulations or order ceasing to have effect does not affect"

-- ---- s 1292 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18552 | (2) Any provision that may be made by regulations under this Act may be made by order; and any provision that may be made by order under this Act may be made by regulations.
@ref s 1292(2) Regulations and orders: supplementary (src:18552)
GIVEN `the provision may be made by regulations under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1292(2) the provision may be made by order` MEANS
    IF `the provision may be made by regulations under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any provision that may be made by regulations under this Act may be made by order"

@ref s 1292(2) Regulations and orders: supplementary (src:18552)
GIVEN `the provision may be made by order under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1292(2) the provision may be made by regulations` MEANS
    IF `the provision may be made by order under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any provision that may be made by order under this Act may be made by regulations"

-- src:18553 | (3) Any provision that may be made by regulations or order under this Act for which no Parliamentary procedure is prescribed may be made by regulations or order subject to negative or affirmative resolution procedure.
@ref s 1292(3) Regulations and orders: supplementary (src:18553)
GIVEN `the provision may be made by regulations or order under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no Parliamentary procedure is prescribed for the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      procedure IS A `s 1288 procedure for regulations or orders`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1292(3) the provision may be made subject to the procedure` MEANS
    IF `the provision may be made by regulations or order under this Act` AND `no Parliamentary procedure is prescribed for the provision`
    THEN CONSIDER procedure
         WHEN `s 1289 negative resolution procedure` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be made by regulations or order subject to negative or affirmative resolution procedure"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for which no Parliamentary procedure is prescribed"

-- src:18554 | (4) Any provision that may be made by regulations or order under this Act subject to negative resolution procedure may be made by regulations or order subject to affirmative resolution procedure.
@ref s 1292(4) Regulations and orders: supplementary (src:18554)
GIVEN `the provision may be made by regulations or order under this Act subject to negative resolution procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1292(4) the provision may be made subject to affirmative resolution procedure` MEANS
    IF `the provision may be made by regulations or order under this Act subject to negative resolution procedure`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any provision that may be made by regulations or order under this Act subject to negative resolution procedure"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1292A: "Bank of England"
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18557 | In this Act, except in section 796, references to the Bank of England do not include the Bank acting in its capacity as the Prudential Regulation Authority.
@ref s 1292A Bank of England (src:18557)
GIVEN `the reference is in section 796` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Bank is acting in its capacity as the Prudential Regulation Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1292A the reference to the Bank of England includes the Bank acting as the Prudential Regulation Authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the reference is in section 796`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in section 796"
        IF `the Bank is acting in its capacity as the Prudential Regulation Authority`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to the Bank of England do not include the Bank acting in its capacity as the Prudential Regulation Authority"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section says what the reference does not include, not what it includes

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1293: meaning of "enactment"
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 1293 kind of provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 1293(a) an enactment contained in subordinate legislation within the meaning of the Interpretation Act 1978`
    `s 1293(aa) an enactment contained in, or in an instrument made under, a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales`
    `s 1293(b) an enactment contained in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament`
    `s 1293(c) an enactment contained in, or in an instrument made under, Northern Ireland legislation within the meaning of the Interpretation Act 1978`
    `s 1293 another kind of provision`

-- src:18560 | In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires, “enactment” includes—
-- src:18561 | (a) an enactment contained in subordinate legislation within the meaning of the Interpretation Act 1978 (c. 30),
-- src:18562 | (aa) an enactment contained in, or in an instrument made under, a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales,
-- src:18563 | (b) an enactment contained in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament, and
-- src:18564 | (c) an enactment contained in, or in an instrument made under, Northern Ireland legislation within the meaning of the Interpretation Act 1978.
@ref s 1293 Meaning of "enactment" (src:18560-18564)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1293 kind of provision`
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1293 the provision is an enactment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF kind EQUALS `s 1293 another kind of provision`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“enactment” includes"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- =========================================================================================================
-- ss 1294 to 1297: consequential and transitional provisions
-- =========================================================================================================

-- The procedure that the text itself attaches to orders under ss 1294 and 1296 (and, below, to the regulations
-- and orders in ss 1277, 1281 (241A(4)(c)) and Schedules 1A and 1B).
-- src:18578 | (6) Orders under this section are subject to affirmative resolution procedure.
@ref s 1294(6) Power to make consequential amendments etc (src:18578)
GIVETH A `s 1288 procedure for regulations or orders`
`s 1294(6) the procedure for an order under section 1294` MEANS `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure`

-- src:18585 | (4) Orders under this section are subject to negative resolution procedure.
@ref s 1296(4) Power to make transitional provision and savings (src:18585)
GIVETH A `s 1288 procedure for regulations or orders`
`s 1296(4) the procedure for an order under section 1296` MEANS `s 1289 negative resolution procedure`

-- ---- s 1297: continuity of the law ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18587 | (1) This section applies where any provision of this Act re-enacts (with or without modification) an enactment repealed by this Act.
@ref s 1297(1) Continuity of the law (src:18587)
GIVEN `a provision of this Act re-enacts (with or without modification) an enactment repealed by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1297(1) section 1297 applies` MEANS
    IF `a provision of this Act re-enacts (with or without modification) an enactment repealed by this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where any provision of this Act re-enacts (with or without modification) an enactment repealed by this Act"

-- src:18588 | (2) The repeal and re-enactment does not affect the continuity of the law.
@ref s 1297(2) Continuity of the law (src:18588)
GIVEN `section 1297 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1297(2) the repeal and re-enactment affects the continuity of the law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `section 1297 applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The repeal and re-enactment does not affect the continuity of the law"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where"

-- src:18592 | (6) This section has effect subject to any specific transitional provision or saving contained in this Act.
@ref s 1297(6) Continuity of the law (src:18592)
GIVEN `a specific transitional provision or saving contained in this Act applies to the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1297(6) section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` MEANS
    IF `a specific transitional provision or saving contained in this Act applies to the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section has effect subject to any specific transitional provision or saving contained in this Act"

-- src:18589 | (3) Anything done (including subordinate legislation made), or having effect as if done, under or for the purposes of the repealed provision that could have been done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision of this Act, if in force or effective immediately before the commencement of that corresponding provision, has effect thereafter as if done under or for the purposes of that corresponding provision.
@ref s 1297(3) Continuity of the law (src:18589)
GIVEN `section 1297 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing was done (including subordinate legislation made), or has effect as if done, under or for the purposes of the repealed provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it could have been done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision of this Act, if in force or effective immediately before the commencement of that corresponding provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1297(3) the thing has effect thereafter as if done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision of this Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 1297 applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" (subsection (1) fails)
        IF `section 1297 applies` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a provision of this Act re-enacts a repealed enactment is not answered here
        IF `section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section has effect subject to any specific transitional provision or saving contained in this Act"
        IF `the thing was done (including subordinate legislation made), or has effect as if done, under or for the purposes of the repealed provision` AND `it could have been done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision of this Act, if in force or effective immediately before the commencement of that corresponding provision`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Anything done ... that could have been done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision"

-- src:18590 | (4) Any reference (express or implied) in this Act or any other enactment, instrument or document to a provision of this Act shall be construed (so far as the context permits) as including, as respects times, circumstances or purposes in relation to which the corresponding repealed provision had effect, a reference to that corresponding provision.
@ref s 1297(4) Continuity of the law (src:18590)
GIVEN `section 1297 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the reference (express or implied) is to a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context permits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time, circumstance or purpose is one in relation to which the corresponding repealed provision had effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1297(4) the reference to the provision of this Act is construed as including a reference to the corresponding repealed provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 1297 applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" (subsection (1) fails)
        IF `section 1297 applies` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a provision of this Act re-enacts a repealed enactment is not answered here
        IF `section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section has effect subject to any specific transitional provision or saving contained in this Act"
        IF NOT (`the context permits`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(so far as the context permits)"
        IF `the reference (express or implied) is to a provision of this Act` AND `the time, circumstance or purpose is one in relation to which the corresponding repealed provision had effect`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as respects times, circumstances or purposes in relation to which the corresponding repealed provision had effect"

-- src:18591 | (5) Any reference (express or implied) in any enactment, instrument or document to a repealed provision shall be construed (so far as the context permits), as respects times, circumstances and purposes in relation to which the corresponding provision of this Act has effect, as being or (according to the context) including a reference to the corresponding provision of this Act.
@ref s 1297(5) Continuity of the law (src:18591)
GIVEN `section 1297 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the reference (express or implied) is to a repealed provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context permits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time, circumstance or purpose is one in relation to which the corresponding provision of this Act has effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1297(5) the reference to the repealed provision is construed as being or including a reference to the corresponding provision of this Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 1297 applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" (subsection (1) fails)
        IF `section 1297 applies` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a provision of this Act re-enacts a repealed enactment is not answered here
        IF `section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section has effect subject to any specific transitional provision or saving contained in this Act"
        IF NOT (`the context permits`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(so far as the context permits)"
        IF `the reference (express or implied) is to a repealed provision` AND `the time, circumstance or purpose is one in relation to which the corresponding provision of this Act has effect`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as respects times, circumstances and purposes in relation to which the corresponding provision of this Act has effect"

-- src:18593 | (7) References in this section to this Act include subordinate legislation made under this Act.
@ref s 1297(7) Continuity of the law (src:18593)
GIVEN `the reference is in section 1297` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is subordinate legislation made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1297(7) the reference to this Act includes the instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the reference is in section 1297`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References in this section to this Act"
        IF `the instrument is subordinate legislation made under this Act`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include subordinate legislation made under this Act"

-- src:18594 | (8) In this section “subordinate legislation” has the same meaning as in the Interpretation Act 1978 (c. 30).
@ref s 1297(8) Continuity of the law (src:18594)
GIVEN `the instrument is subordinate legislation within the meaning of the Interpretation Act 1978` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1297(8) the instrument is subordinate legislation for section 1297` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the instrument is subordinate legislation within the meaning of the Interpretation Act 1978`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the borrowed definition says no, supplied as an input): "“subordinate legislation” has the same meaning as in the Interpretation Act 1978"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act 1978 is not among the sources
